From 6d756b2c41421f70319aa430394297dfb9a59788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] tests/http_head: drop the public-site HEAD checks

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 CI runner here has no general internet egress for arbitrary public-site HTTP]

test.py's test_sites tuple HEADs google.com/twitter.com/douban.com/
github.com over plain port-80 HTTP alongside the local fake slow
server, to prove the patched C extension's blocking connect/send/recv
don't block the gevent hub even against real external hosts. That
needs outbound internet access to specific third-party sites from the
CI container, which this repo's riscv64 runners aren't provisioned
for, and would make the job flaky against hosts we don't control
either way.

The local_addr case already exercises the exact same code path
(greenify.patch_lib() against mod_http_head, then concurrent
gevent.spawn() of the C and the plain-Python HEAD check against a
real blocking server) and is what the elapsed-time assertion is
actually checking, so it alone keeps the test meaningful.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 tests/http_head/test.py | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/http_head/test.py b/tests/http_head/test.py
index c95f947..ca2bb19 100644
--- a/tests/http_head/test.py
+++ b/tests/http_head/test.py
@@ -62,10 +62,6 @@ def main():
     local_addr = ("localhost", str(fake_slow_http_server.PORT))
     test_sites = (
         local_addr,
-        ("google.com", "80"),
-        ("twitter.com", "80"),
-        ("douban.com", "80"),
-        ("github.com", "80"),
     )
     for fn in [python_http_head_check, c_http_head_check]:
         stack = []
